    <node id="action">
      <data key="d0">action</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c03a55d3ed535c691cb634704db74a30-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-14ceb1ebb14936f5b21a23a880dfeaca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-37efc5c1445ce192ca1d962c1d8c91dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-461bb085df60d40466f8b6722f80c025-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6371d7766d8a30a1d8aedfb05c069ba8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fdd8eb5fe9d7ea8984fec9eb6c4e6878-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-189de8ba1f681a4ac020519f647f3544-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3df8bd91a6a3d0871e38317475d7b157-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5c82ff2039f325fb23b86afa8c23dcf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-641918b0c83a0a355d25025600a88524-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-756d823b08bd1c3abebceb95e49c808b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a27c3607ebcd1cbf634c7919d8b8e521-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d2">Action refers to a step or operation performed during a task or process. It can involve clicking, as mentioned in the first description, and it is often executed by either a user or a system. Actions are integral parts of tasks and processes, serving as maneuvers or operations that contribute to achieving specific goals. Whether it's a simple click or a more complex maneuver, actions are fundamental components of any task or process, ensuring that tasks are carried out efficiently and effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;The action performed during the task.&lt;SEP&gt;An operation performed as part of a task.</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1787056245</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
